 edge. Barringer's strong fundraising and an opinion piece noting Trump's softening approval in red North Carolina districts justify only a modest tightening from the ratings-implied margin.", "watch": "Any general-election polling showing Barringer within single digits, or further evidence of Republican erosion in North Carolina, could move this toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Brad Knott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 13th District leans Republican by about eight points, and first-term Representative Brad Knott is seeking reelection with roughly $700,000 on hand. Democratic nominee Paul Barringer, a Sanford-area candidate focused on health care and agriculture, has run a serious campaign, raising over $1 million, but enters as a clear underdog in a district drawn to favor Republicans.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on district fundamentals and expert assessments. Ratings from ten outlets cluster between Likely R and Solid R, and prediction markets give Knott roughly an 83% chance. Knott has also publicized legislative wins, including a veterans' home bill for Harnett County. The race remains Likely Republican, with Barringer needing a significant national environment shift to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0835, "margin": -8.64}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1064, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1381, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0942, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0796, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1209, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1113, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem":